WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.220
Add a growth factor to a resting cell, and within minutes it is transcribing a gene

2
00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.660
called c-fos. Now use a drug to stop every ribosome in the cell.

3
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.720
The gene still switches on.

4
00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.940
So whatever switched it on was already made, and waiting.

5
00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.240
What was waiting there, and what did the signal do to it?

6
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.870
A transcription factor is a protein that binds a short DNA sequence near a gene.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:32.310
Making more of a factor is slow, so fast gene responses usually change one already

8
00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:34.830
made. One such factor is CREB.

9
00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:39.830
It sits in front of c-fos as a pair, largely there before any signal arrives.

10
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.430
Yet being on the DNA is not enough to switch the gene on.

11
00:00:44.483 --> 00:00:50.343
When cAMP rises, it frees the catalytic subunits of a kinase called PKA.

12
00:00:50.343 --> 00:00:51.943
Some of them enter the nucleus.

13
00:00:52.703 --> 00:00:57.163
There PKA puts a phosphate on one serine of CREB, serine 133.

14
00:00:58.123 --> 00:01:01.423
That phosphate is a handle, something another protein can hold.

15
00:01:02.483 --> 00:01:06.503
A co-activator is a helper protein that does not bind DNA itself.

16
00:01:07.243 --> 00:01:10.563
The co-activator CBP has a small domain called KIX.

17
00:01:11.203 --> 00:01:14.143
KIX grips CREB far more tightly when the phosphate is on.

18
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:20.363
Held at the gene, CBP adds acetyl groups to the histones that package DNA, which

19
00:01:20.363 --> 00:01:25.263
loosens them. It also contacts the machinery that brings in RNA polymerase.

20
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:28.373
Now take a different messenger, calcium.

21
00:01:29.193 --> 00:01:33.853
Calcium and calmodulin, helped by an upstream kinase, switch on CaMKIV.

22
00:01:34.473 --> 00:01:38.913
This kinase is found largely in the nucleus, and it phosphorylates CREB on the same

23
00:01:38.913 --> 00:01:43.533
serine. So CREB is a place where messengers meet, and either one adds the same

24
00:01:43.533 --> 00:01:49.473
handle. Growth factors reach that serine too, through kinases that ERK switches on.

25
00:01:50.517 --> 00:01:52.677
Now go back to the gene, c-fos.

26
00:01:53.277 --> 00:01:55.617
Its control region carries a site for CREB.

27
00:01:56.597 --> 00:02:01.577
cAMP, calcium and growth factors can each reach the gene through factors already in

28
00:02:01.577 --> 00:02:04.537
place. That is why the ribosomes did not matter.

29
00:02:05.017 --> 00:02:09.557
So keep this rule: the factor is already made, and the signal changes what it does.
